cmuzniisi09ezgeetw8qbh0nc	Neumann TLM 103 Large-Diaphragm Cardioid Condenser Studio Microphone	neumann-tlm-103-condenser-studio-microphone	NEUMANN-TLM-103-CONDENSER-STUDIO-MICROPH	<p>The Neumann TLM 103 is a large-diaphragm condenser microphone that delivers the signature Neumann sound with enhanced presence to deliver a clear, clean, and full tone. It has a U 87-based capsule coupled with faultless transformerless circuitry, enabling it to tolerate high SPLs of up to 138 dB without distortion while keeping very low self-noise of about 7 dBA. The combination of the transformerless output stage and heightened treble response makes the TLM 103 a great choice when the sound source needs to clearly cut through the mix. The mic's compact body is ideal for positioning it in tight spots such as over a snare, inside a kick drum, or in front of a small guitar amp. By utilizing a cardioid polar pattern, the mic can effectively reduce ambient noise or instrument bleed behind the mic. The TLM 103 comes with a secure, space-saving swivel mount and a wooden box.</p><p>The TLM 103, which was first offered in 1997 as a less expensive replacement for the renowned U 87, has subsequently earned a place in the annals of design history. Today, the TLM 103 serves as the benchmark for evaluating modern studio microphones. The TLM 103 has a distinctly Neumann appearance because to its conventional, tapered head grille design.</p><p>The Neumann TLM 103 is a cardioid microphone with a large-diaphragm condenser capsule derived from the classic K67/87 capsule of the legendary Neumann U 87. However, the TLM 103 has a slightly more modern voicing with a wide presence boost for frequencies above 5 kHz.</p><p>Its highly direct yet polished tone is ideal for singers and solo instruments that effortlessly stand out in the mix. The TLM 103, of course, also features the renowned authoritative midrange that has become the distinguishing feature of Neumann microphones and elevated them to a top option i